{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    The sequence is defined by a(1)=1, a(2)=1, and a(n)=a(a(n-1)) + a(n - a(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a list to store sequence terms for memoization, 1-indexed.\n    # seq[0] is unused, seq[i] stores the i-th term a(i).\n    seq = [0] * (n + 1)\n    seq[1] = 1\n    seq[2] = 1\n\n    # Compute terms from a(3) up to a(n) using the recurrence relation.\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        seq[i] = seq[seq[i-1]] + seq[i - seq[i-1]]\n\n    return seq[n]"}
