{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the digits of a number alternate between increasing and decreasing.\n    An undulating number requires at least three digits to establish an alternating pattern.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits = [int(d) for d in str(number)]\n    num_digits = len(digits)\n\n    if num_digits < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Determine the initial trend between the first two digits\n    if digits[0] == digits[1]:\n        return False\n    \n    # True if initial trend is increasing (d0 < d1), False if decreasing (d0 > d1)\n    is_increasing_trend = (digits[0] < digits[1])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the digits to check for alternation\n    for i in range(1, num_digits - 1):\n        current_digit = digits[i]\n        next_digit = digits[i+1]\n\n        if current_digit == next_digit:\n            return False  # Digits must strictly alternate\n\n        if is_increasing_trend:\n            # Previous trend was increasing (e.g., d_{i-1} < d_i), so current trend must be decreasing (d_i > d_{i+1})\n            if current_digit < next_digit:\n                return False  # Pattern broken: expected decreasing, found increasing\n            is_increasing_trend = False # Toggle expected trend for next pair\n        else:\n            # Previous trend was decreasing (e.g., d_{i-1} > d_i), so current trend must be increasing (d_i < d_{i+1})\n            if current_digit > next_digit:\n                return False  # Pattern broken: expected increasing, found decreasing\n            is_increasing_trend = True # Toggle expected trend for next pair\n            \n    return True"}
