{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(items: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the integer that occurs most frequently in `items`.\n    If multiple integers share the same maximum frequency, the first\n    occurring integer in the list is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty\")\n\n    frequency_map = {}\n    max_value = items[0]\n    max_count = 0\n\n    for idx, value in enumerate(items):\n        count = frequency_map.get(value, 0) + 1\n        frequency_map[value] = count\n\n        # Update max only if count is higher or equal but earlier\n        if count > max_count or (count == max_count and idx < items.index(max_value)):\n            max_count = count\n            max_value = value\n\n    return max_value"}
