{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a non-negative integer.\n    Uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficient counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    while number > 0:\n        number &= (number - 1)  # Clears the least significant set bit\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "import bisect\ndef is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_occurrence_idx = bisect.bisect_left(array, element)\n    \n    # If the element is not found at all, it cannot be a majority element\n    if first_occurrence_idx == n or array[first_occurrence_idx] != element:\n        return False\n    \n    last_occurrence_idx_plus_one = bisect.bisect_right(array, element)\n    \n    count = last_occurrence_idx_plus_one - first_occurrence_idx\n    \n    return count > (n // 2)"}
