{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Dict\nclass TuplePair:\n    \"\"\"Represents an an unordered pair of integers, internally storing them sorted for consistent hashing and equality.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, e1: int, e2: int):\n        self.elements = tuple(sorted((e1, e2)))\n\n    def __eq__(self, other):\n        if not isinstance(other, TuplePair):\n            return NotImplemented\n        return self.elements == other.elements\n\n    def __hash__(self):\n        return hash(self.elements)\n\n    def to_tuple(self) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the internal sorted tuple representation of the pair.\"\"\"\n        return self.elements\nclass OccurrenceMap:\n    \"\"\"Manages the counting of unique TuplePair occurrences.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.counts: Dict[TuplePair, int] = {}\n\n    def add(self, pair: TuplePair):\n        \"\"\"Adds an occurrence of a TuplePair, incrementing its count.\"\"\"\n        self.counts[pair] = self.counts.get(pair, 0) + 1\n\n    def get_counts(self) -> Dict[Tuple[int, int], int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a dictionary mapping sorted standard tuples to their accumulated counts.\"\"\"\n        result = {}\n        for pair_obj, count in self.counts.items():\n            result[pair_obj.to_tuple()] = count\n        return result\ndef check_occurences(input_tuples: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> Dict[Tuple[int, int], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of unordered tuples in a list, returning a dictionary of counts.\n    Tuples (a, b) and (b, a) are treated as the same unique tuple, with keys normalized to (min, max).\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrence_map = OccurrenceMap()\n    for tpl in input_tuples:\n        e1, e2 = tpl\n        pair = TuplePair(e1, e2)\n        occurrence_map.add(pair)\n    return occurrence_map.get_counts()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-numbered bits (1-indexed) of the given number `n` to 1.\n    This operation applies to 0-indexed bit positions 1, 3, 5, etc.,\n    up to the bit length of `n`.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_bits = n.bit_length()\n    mask = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through 0-indexed odd bit positions (1, 3, 5, ...)\n    # which correspond to 1-indexed even bit positions (2nd, 4th, 6th, ...).\n    # Construct the mask to cover only up to the bit length of n.\n    current_bit_pos = 1\n    while current_bit_pos < num_bits:\n        mask |= (1 << current_bit_pos)\n        current_bit_pos += 2\n            \n    # Apply the mask using bitwise OR to set the specified bits.\n    return n | mask"}
