{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\nclass LPSCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def lps(input_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(input_str)\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence for substring s[i...j]\n        dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n        \n        # All characters are palindromes of length 1\n        for i in range(n):\n            dp[i][i] = 1\n            \n        # Build the table bottom-up, considering substrings of increasing length\n        for length in range(2, n + 1): # length of substring\n            for i in range(n - length + 1): # starting index\n                j = i + length - 1 # ending index\n                \n                if input_str[i] == input_str[j]:\n                    # If characters at ends match, they contribute 2 to the LPS, \n                    # plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1]\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n                else:\n                    # If characters at ends don't match, the LPS is the maximum of:\n                    # 1. LPS of s[i+1...j] (excluding s[i])\n                    # 2. LPS of s[i...j-1] (excluding s[j])\n                    dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n                    \n        return dp[0][n - 1]\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_string must be a str\")\n    \n    si = StringInput(value=input_string)\n    return LPSCalculator.lps(si.value)"}
