{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than a given non-negative integer n.\n    Uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a boolean array \"is_prime[0..n-1]\" and fill all entries it as true.\n    # A value in is_prime[i] will finally be false if i is Not a prime, else true.\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False  # 0 and 1 are not prime numbers\n\n    for p in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        # If is_prime[p] is still true, then it is a prime\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            # Update all multiples of p\n            for multiple in range(p*p, n, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n\n    # Count all prime numbers\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            count += 1\n\n    return count"}
