{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in an array formed by\n    repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm for max subarray sum in a single array\n    max_single = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        max_single = max(max_single, current_max)\n\n    # If k is 1, the answer is simply max_single\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_single\n\n    # Calculate total sum of the array\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate max prefix sum (max sum starting from index 0)\n    max_prefix = arr[0]\n    current_sum = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_sum += arr[i]\n        max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_sum)\n\n    # Calculate max suffix sum (max sum ending at index n-1)\n    max_suffix = arr[n - 1]\n    current_sum = arr[n - 1]\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        current_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_sum)\n\n    # Initialize overall max sum with the max sum within a single array\n    overall_max = max_single\n\n    # Consider the case where the max subarray spans two copies of the array\n    # e.g., ... [suffix from first copy] + [prefix from second copy] ...\n    overall_max = max(overall_max, max_prefix + max_suffix)\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive, adding more full arrays can increase the sum.\n    # This covers cases where the max subarray spans > 2 blocks.\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        if k > 2:\n            overall_max = max(overall_max, max_prefix + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_suffix)\n\n    return overall_max"}
