{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    l0, l1 = 2, 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = l0 + l1\n        l0 = l1\n        l1 = next_lucas\n    return l1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def convert_list_dictionary(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts three parallel lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Raises ValueError if the input lists have differing lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (len(list1) == len(list2) == len(list3)):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        inner_dict = {list2[i]: list3[i]}\n        outer_dict = {list1[i]: inner_dict}\n        result.append(outer_dict)\n    return result"}
