{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(s: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeated character in a given string using a Clean Architecture-inspired approach.\n    Delegates the core logic to internal TextAnalyzer and CharacterFrequency components.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Nested classes implement the design's components within the function's scope.\n    class CharacterFrequency:\n        \"\"\"Maintains a private dictionary mapping characters to their occurrence counts.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self):\n            self._frequency_map = {}\n\n        def add(self, char: str) -> None:\n            \"\"\"Increments the count for char.\"\"\"\n            self._frequency_map[char] = self._frequency_map.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n        def get(self, char: str) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Retrieves the current count for char.\"\"\"\n            return self._frequency_map.get(char, 0)\n\n    class TextAnalyzer:\n        \"\"\"Uses a CharacterFrequency instance to compute the first non-repeating character.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, character_frequency: CharacterFrequency = None):\n            self._character_frequency = character_frequency if character_frequency is not None else CharacterFrequency()\n\n        def find_first_non_repeating_character(self, input_string: str) -> Optional[str]:\n            \"\"\"\n            Iterates over input, adding only alphabetic characters to the frequency map.\n            Then iterates again in order, returning the first character whose count is 1.\n            \"\"\"\n            # First pass: populate frequency map\n            for char in input_string:\n                if char.isalpha():\n                    self._character_frequency.add(char)\n\n            # Second pass: find the first non-repeating character\n            for char in input_string:\n                if char.isalpha() and self._character_frequency.get(char) == 1:\n                    return char\n            return None\n\n    # The public API creates an analyzer and delegates the call.\n    # Note: 'Optional' type hint assumes 'from typing import Optional' is available in the execution environment.\n    analyzer = TextAnalyzer()\n    return analyzer.find_first_non_repeating_character(s)"}
