{"task_id": "Mbpp/420", "solution": "def cube_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first n even natural numbers.\n    This function uses NumberSequence and CubeSumCalculator classes for its internal logic.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class NumberSequence:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates the first n even natural numbers.\n        \"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, n_val: int):\n            self.n = n_val\n\n        def iter_even_numbers(self):\n            \"\"\"\n            Yields even numbers from 2 up to 2*n.\n            \"\"\"\n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                yield 2 * i\n\n    class CubeSumCalculator:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the sum of cubes for a given sequence of numbers.\n        \"\"\"\n        def calculate(self, n_val: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"\n            Calculates the sum of cubes of the first n even natural numbers.\n            \"\"\"\n            total_sum = 0\n            # According to the class diagram and sequence diagram, CubeSumCalculator uses NumberSequence.\n            number_sequence = NumberSequence(n_val)\n            for even_num in number_sequence.iter_even_numbers():\n                total_sum += even_num ** 3\n            return total_sum\n\n    calculator = CubeSumCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate(n)"}
