{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\ndef index_multiplication(a: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...], b: Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]) -> Tuple[Tuple[int, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements within two tuples of tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if input tuples have mismatched shapes.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of inner tuples.\")\n\n    result_inner_tuples = []\n    for inner_tuple_a, inner_tuple_b in zip(a, b):\n        if len(inner_tuple_a) != len(inner_tuple_b):\n            raise ValueError(\"All corresponding inner tuples must have the same length.\")\n        \n        multiplied_elements = tuple(element_a * element_b for element_a, element_b in zip(inner_tuple_a, inner_tuple_b))\n        result_inner_tuples.append(multiplied_elements)\n\n    return tuple(result_inner_tuples)"}
