{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given number n.\n    For n >= 5, the last digit of n! is always 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0  # Factorial not defined for negative numbers, returning 0 as per typical contest behavior\n    elif n < 5:\n        # Calculate factorial and take modulo 10\n        factorial_val = 1\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            factorial_val *= i\n        return factorial_val % 10\n    else:\n        # For n >= 5, n! will always end in 0\n        return 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(list_a, list_b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if list_b is a contiguous sublist of list_a using a sliding window.\n    Assumes valid list inputs based on design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    n, m = len(list_a), len(list_b)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True\n    if n == 0 or m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if list_a[i:i+m] == list_b:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "def find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a tuple containing elements that are present in one of the input tuples\n    but not in both (symmetric difference).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    try:\n        set1 = set(tuple1)\n        set2 = set(tuple2)\n    except TypeError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements must be hashable.\") from exc\n\n    diff = set1.symmetric_difference(set2)\n    return tuple(diff)"}
