{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is one whose sum of digits raised to the power of the number of digits is equal to the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    class Number:\n        def __init__(self, value):\n            self.value = value\n\n        def isArmstrong(self):\n            if self.value < 0:\n                return False  # Negative numbers are treated as non-Armstrong.\n            if self.value == 0:\n                return True\n\n            str_value = str(self.value)\n            num_digits = len(str_value)\n            armstrong_sum = 0\n            for digit_char in str_value:\n                digit = int(digit_char)\n                armstrong_sum += digit ** num_digits\n            return armstrong_sum == self.value\n\n    num_obj = Number(number)\n    return num_obj.isArmstrong()"}
