{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(arr1, arr2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element from two given sorted arrays.\n    Uses a binary search approach on the smaller array.\n    \"\"\"\n    m, n = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n\n    # Ensure arr1 is the smaller array to perform binary search on it\n    if m > n:\n        arr1, arr2 = arr2, arr1\n        m, n = n, m\n\n    # Define the search space for partition1 (number of elements taken from arr1)\n    # low: Minimum possible elements from arr1 (k - n, or 0 if k <= n)\n    # high: Maximum possible elements from arr1 (k, or m if k > m)\n    low = max(0, k - n)\n    high = min(m, k)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        # partition1 is the number of elements from arr1 in the left part\n        partition1 = (low + high) // 2\n        # partition2 is the number of elements from arr2 in the left part\n        partition2 = k - partition1\n\n        # Get the elements at the boundaries of the partitions\n        # left1 is the last element of arr1's left part\n        # right1 is the first element of arr1's right part\n        # left2 is the last element of arr2's left part\n        # right2 is the first element of arr2's right part\n        \n        # Use -float('inf') for virtual elements before the start of an array\n        # Use float('inf') for virtual elements after the end of an array\n        left1 = arr1[partition1 - 1] if partition1 > 0 else -float('inf')\n        right1 = arr1[partition1] if partition1 < m else float('inf')\n\n        left2 = arr2[partition2 - 1] if partition2 > 0 else -float('inf')\n        right2 = arr2[partition2] if partition2 < n else float('inf')\n\n        # Check if the partitions are correct\n        if left1 <= right2 and left2 <= right1:\n            # We found the correct partition\n            # The k-th element is the maximum of the elements at the partition boundary\n            return max(left1, left2)\n        elif left1 > right2:\n            # partition1 is too large, meaning we took too many from arr1\n            # Adjust high to search in the left half\n            high = partition1 - 1\n        else:  # left2 > right1\n            # partition1 is too small, meaning we took too few from arr1\n            # Adjust low to search in the right half\n            low = partition1 + 1"}
