{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle dynamic programming method.\n    The Bell number B_n is the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the j-th element of the i-th row of the Bell triangle.\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (dp[n][0]) in this construction.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Initialize the first element of the Bell triangle (B_0)\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle row by row\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i-1][i-1]\n        # Fill the remaining elements of the current row using the recurrence relation\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + dp[i][j-1]\n    \n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return dp[n][0]"}
