{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset where every pair of numbers is divisible.\n    The algorithm uses dynamic programming after sorting the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    numbers.sort()\n    dp = [1] * n\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n    \n    return max(dp)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size n.\n    This implementation finds the two middle elements in O(n) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n    \n    med1 = 0  # Will store the (n-1)-th element of the conceptual merged list\n    med2 = 0  # Will store the n-th element of the conceptual merged list\n\n    # Iterate n + 1 times to find the elements that would be at conceptual indices (n-1) and n\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        # Store the previous candidate for med2 into med1\n        med1 = med2 \n        \n        # Determine the next smallest element from either list1 or list2\n        if i < n and j < n:\n            if list1[i] < list2[j]:\n                med2 = list1[i]\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                med2 = list2[j]\n                j += 1\n        elif i < n:  # If list2 is exhausted\n            med2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif j < n:  # If list1 is exhausted\n            med2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n            \n    # The median for 2n elements is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th smallest elements.\n    # In 0-indexed terms, these are the elements at indices n-1 and n.\n    # med1 holds the element at index n-1, and med2 holds the element at index n.\n    return float(med1 + med2) / 2.0"}
