{"task_id": "Mbpp/643", "solution": "import re\ndef text_match_wordz_middle(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string contains 'z' (case-insensitive) in the middle of any word.\n    A 'z' is considered in the middle if it is not the first or last character of a word.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Tokenize the string into words. Words are sequences of alphanumeric characters.\n    words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', text)\n\n    for word in words:\n        # Convert the word to lowercase for case-insensitive checking.\n        lower_word = word.lower()\n        \n        # Iterate through the word, skipping the first and last characters.\n        # This range naturally handles words too short to have a middle 'z'.\n        for i in range(1, len(lower_word) - 1):\n            if lower_word[i] == 'z':\n                return True  # Found a 'z' in the middle of a word\n                \n    return False  # No middle 'z' found in any word"}
