{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "def extract_quotation(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    # Placeholder for escaped double quotes to prevent them from acting as delimiters.\n    # This ensures that only unescaped quotes toggle the 'in_quote' state.\n    ESCAPED_QUOTE_PLACEHOLDER = '\\x1A'\n\n    # Pre-processing: Temporarily replace escaped quotes with the placeholder.\n    processed_text = text.replace('\\\\\"', ESCAPED_QUOTE_PLACEHOLDER)\n\n    results = []\n    in_quote = False\n    current_segment_chars = []\n\n    for char in processed_text:\n        if char == '\"':\n            in_quote = not in_quote\n            if not in_quote:  # Just exited a quoted segment\n                # Join characters to form the segment and add to results.\n                results.append(\"\".join(current_segment_chars))\n                current_segment_chars = []\n        elif in_quote:\n            # Accumulate characters if currently inside a quoted segment.\n            current_segment_chars.append(char)\n\n    # Post-processing: Restore original double quotes from placeholders in captured segments.\n    final_results = [s.replace(ESCAPED_QUOTE_PLACEHOLDER, '\"') for s in results]\n\n    return final_results"}
