{"task_id": "Mbpp/796", "solution": "def return_sum(dictionary: Dict[str, Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the sum of all numeric values in a dictionary.\n    Raises ValueError if any value in the dictionary is not an int or float.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for key, value in dictionary.items():\n        if not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Non-numeric value for key '{key}': {value!r}\")\n        total += value\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l, r):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of all odd natural numbers within the range l and r (inclusive).\n    \"\"\"\n    if l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Find the first odd number greater than or equal to l\n    first_odd = l if l % 2 != 0 else l + 1\n\n    # Find the last odd number less than or equal to r\n    last_odd = r if r % 2 != 0 else r - 1\n\n    # If the effective range of odd numbers is empty, return 0\n    if first_odd > last_odd:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the number of odd terms in the range [first_odd, last_odd]\n    # This is an arithmetic progression with a common difference of 2.\n    count = (last_odd - first_odd) // 2 + 1\n\n    # Use the sum of an arithmetic series formula: n * (a_1 + a_n) / 2\n    total_sum = count * (first_odd + last_odd) // 2\n\n    return total_sum"}
