{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number, d):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number left by d positions.\n    The rotation wraps around, ensuring the result is also 32-bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_bits = 32\n    shift = d % num_bits\n    \n    # Handle the case where the effective shift is 0\n    if shift == 0:\n        return number & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    # Perform the left rotation: (bits shifted left) OR (bits shifted right from overflow)\n    rotated_value = ((number << shift) | (number >> (num_bits - shift)))\n    \n    # Mask to ensure the result remains within 32 bits\n    return rotated_value & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "import math\ndef is_perfect_square(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a perfect square. Returns False for negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    root = math.isqrt(number)\n    return root * root == number"}
