{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef max_sum_list(list_of_lists: List[List[int]]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the sublist from a list of lists whose elements sum to the highest value.\n    Assumes valid input: a non-empty list of non-empty lists of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_sum = None\n    max_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_sum = sum(sublist)\n        if max_sum is None or current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            max_sublist = sublist\n\n    return max_sublist"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "def max_run_uppercase(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum run of uppercase characters in the given string.\n    Iterates through the string, tracking the current and maximum consecutive uppercase runs.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n    for char in input_string:\n        if 'A' <= char <= 'Z':  # Check if the character is an uppercase letter\n            current_run += 1\n        else:\n            current_run = 0\n        max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n    return max_run"}
