{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n\n    Returns a new list, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n    \n    n = len(lst)\n    k = count % n\n    \n    return lst[-k:] + lst[:-k]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    This algorithm runs in O(n) time and O(1) space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = array[0]\n    min_so_far = array[0]\n    global_max = array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        x = array[i]\n\n        # Store the current max_so_far and min_so_far to use for calculations\n        # before they are updated for the current element.\n        prev_max_so_far = max_so_far\n        prev_min_so_far = min_so_far\n\n        # If the current number is positive, it can extend both max_so_far and min_so_far.\n        # If negative, multiplying by a negative flips the max/min roles.\n        if x >= 0:\n            max_so_far = max(x, prev_max_so_far * x)\n            min_so_far = min(x, prev_min_so_far * x)\n        else:  # x < 0\n            # A negative number makes a small negative product large positive,\n            # and a large positive product small negative.\n            max_so_far = max(x, prev_min_so_far * x)\n            min_so_far = min(x, prev_max_so_far * x)\n\n        global_max = max(global_max, max_so_far)\n\n    return global_max"}
